{"id":8188725,"docketId":65286466,"caseName":"Chubb v. Washington","caseNameFull":"Chubb v. Washington","slug":"chubb-v-washington","docketNumber":"No. 288","dateFiled":"1934-10-08","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1934,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. Paul Cassel Chubb, pro se. Mr. Charles W. Greenough for respondent.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8150656,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":2004,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"Ae1\">\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"ADYu\">The motion of the appellee to dismiss the appeal herein is granted, and the appeal is dismissed for the want of a properly presented federal question. <em>Kerr Glass Mfg. Corp. </em>v. <em>Superior Court, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8148937\"><a href=\"/opinion/8187007/kerr-glass-mfg-corp-v-superior-court/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Kerr Glass Mfg. Corp. v. Superior Court\">286 U. S. 532</a></span>; <em>White River Co. </em>v. <em>Arkansas, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9418681\"><a href=\"/opinion/101448/white-river-lumber-co-v-arkansas-ex-rel-applegate/#700\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: White River Lumber Co. v. Arkansas Ex Rel. Applegate\">279 U. S. 692, 700</a></span>; <em>Hiawassee River Power Co. </em>v. <em>Carolina-Tennessee Power Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99550\"><a href=\"/opinion/99550/hiawassee-river-power-co-v-carolina-tennessee-power-co/#344\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Hiawassee River Power Co. v. Carolina-Tennessee Power Co.\">252 U. S. 341, 344</a></span>; <em>Cleveland &amp; Pittsburgh R. Co. </em>v. <em>Cleveland, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98274\"><a href=\"/opinion/98274/cleveland-pittsburgh-railroad-v-city-of-cleveland/#53\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Cleveland &amp; Pittsburgh Railroad v. City of Cleveland\">235 U. S. 50, 53</a></span>; <em>Manhattan Life Ins. Co. </em>v. <em>Cohen, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98212\"><a href=\"/opinion/98212/manhattan-life-ins-co-of-ny-v-cohen/#134\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Manhattan Life Ins. Co. of NY v. Cohen\">234 U. S. 123, 134</a></span>; <em>Chapin </em>v. <em>Fye, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9417826\"><a href=\"/opinion/95344/chapin-v-fye/#129\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Chapin v. Fye\">179 U. S. 127, 129, 130</a></span>. The motion for leave to proceed further herein <em>in forma pauperis </em>is denied.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}